# --- Client data (NEVER commit) ---
# This repository is public. Real client data must not leave the machine, so the
# whole directory is ignored rather than named files — an ignore list that has to
# be updated per file is one that eventually misses one.
#
# The README is kept so the folder's purpose is in the repo while its contents
# stay out. Anything derived from this data — extracts, fixtures, seed scripts
# with real rows pasted in — belongs here too, not in backend/ or docs/.
#
# Written as `/data/*` and not `/data/`: excluding the directory itself stops git
# descending into it, and a negation inside a directory git never enters has no
# effect — the README would silently stay ignored.
/data/*
!/data/README.md
